From 4c8b728d34f43151b44a6dbaf7b4ad4f72496bff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diogo Casteluber Laass <4793368+iowaz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:07:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] TrickyStore: Don't attest an all-zero verified boot key
 as Verified

hackAttestExtension() takes the verified boot key from the TEE's own
RootOfTrust and falls back to AttestationUtils.getBootKey() only when
that octet string is missing or empty. It then always writes
deviceLocked=true and verifiedBootState=Verified.

klimt's TEE attests a 32-byte all-zero boot key while the bootloader is
unlocked (Duck Detector, 2026-10-20: Unverified, deviceLocked false,
boot key 00..00). That key is not empty, so every leaf- or auto-hacked
key would claim a locked, Verified device with an all-zero boot key,
a combination AOSP only allows for Unverified, and upstream now also
persists that chain at key generation. The generated-key path
(CertificateGenerator) already uses AttestationUtils.getBootKey().

Treat an all-zero key like a missing one. The boot hash is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../security/trickystore/CertificateHacker.java    | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/java/android/security/trickystore/CertificateHacker.java b/core/java/android/security/trickystore/CertificateHacker.java
index 1639ada403d0..b57db44dc108 100644
--- a/core/java/android/security/trickystore/CertificateHacker.java
+++ b/core/java/android/security/trickystore/CertificateHacker.java
@@ -360,7 +360,10 @@ public final class CertificateHacker {
             String[] packages) throws Exception {
 
         byte[] bootKey = rootOfTrustOctet(originalRootOfTrust, 0);
-        if (bootKey == null) {
+        // An unlocked bootloader can make the TEE attest an all-zero verified boot key, which is
+        // only valid with an Unverified boot state. The hacked RootOfTrust says Verified, so use
+        // the same boot key as the generated path instead.
+        if (bootKey == null || isAllZero(bootKey)) {
             bootKey = AttestationUtils.getBootKey();
         }
 
@@ -422,6 +425,15 @@ public final class CertificateHacker {
         return new Extension(CertificateGenerator.ATTESTATION_OID, false, hackedOctets);
     }
 
+    private static boolean isAllZero(byte[] value) {
+        for (byte b : value) {
+            if (b != 0) {
+                return false;
+            }
+        }
+        return true;
+    }
+
     private static byte[] rootOfTrustOctet(ASN1Encodable rootOfTrust, int index) {
         try {
             ASN1Sequence sequence = ASN1Sequence.getInstance(rootOfTrust);
